WEBVTT

00:00:00.362 --> 00:00:02.537
Here's a bath filling with the plug out.

00:00:03.141 --> 00:00:05.101
The tap runs in and the drain takes

00:00:05.182 --> 00:00:05.641
water out,

00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:08.022
so this graph is the net flow,

00:00:08.623 --> 00:00:11.524
twelve minus two t litres per minute, over

00:00:11.625 --> 00:00:14.625
eight minutes, with thin rectangles one minute wide.

00:00:15.587 --> 00:00:18.352
Positive means the bath is gaining water, and

00:00:18.494 --> 00:00:20.197
negative means it's losing water.

00:00:21.001 --> 00:00:23.248
The tap is being turned down, so after

00:00:23.309 --> 00:00:25.315
six minutes the drain wins, and the net

00:00:25.356 --> 00:00:26.338
flow is negative.

00:00:27.424 --> 00:00:28.048
Think for a moment.

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:30.860
What could a strip below the axis mean?

00:00:31.926 --> 00:00:33.021
Look at the last rectangle.

00:00:33.486 --> 00:00:35.536
Its height is minus two, and its width

00:00:35.678 --> 00:00:36.361
is one minute.

00:00:37.065 --> 00:00:39.290
Minus two litres per minute, times one minute,

00:00:39.452 --> 00:00:40.714
is minus two litres.

00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:43.585
So the bath lost roughly two litres.

00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:46.455
So a strip below the axis is a

00:00:46.636 --> 00:00:47.378
negative change.

00:00:48.029 --> 00:00:49.744
So keep every strip's sign.

00:00:50.168 --> 00:00:53.075
Strips above the axis add, and strips below

00:00:53.137 --> 00:00:54.239
the axis subtract.

00:00:54.842 --> 00:00:56.450
That makes it a signed sum.

00:00:57.317 --> 00:00:59.191
Now refine it, just as we did before.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:03.143
With sixteen strips, the signed sum is thirty-six.

00:01:03.807 --> 00:01:05.554
With sixty-four, it's thirty-three.

00:01:06.137 --> 00:01:08.544
With two hundred and fifty-six, it's thirty-two point

00:01:08.605 --> 00:01:09.146
two five.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:11.544
Now use the right ends instead.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.145
The sums are twenty-eight, thirty-one, and thirty-one point

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:15.829
seven five.

00:01:16.553 --> 00:01:18.639
Both sets close in on the same number,

00:01:19.082 --> 00:01:19.542
thirty-two.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.632
However we choose the heights,

00:01:22.156 --> 00:01:24.205
thinner strips settle on one value.

00:01:24.822 --> 00:01:27.052
That settled number gets its own name,

00:01:27.655 --> 00:01:29.021
the definite integral.

00:01:29.745 --> 00:01:31.975
We write it with this long S, which

00:01:32.136 --> 00:01:32.840
stands for sum.

00:01:33.663 --> 00:01:35.587
The integral from a to b of f

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:36.850
of x, d x,

00:01:37.413 --> 00:01:39.317
is the limit of the sums of f

00:01:39.338 --> 00:01:41.963
of x times delta x, as delta x

00:01:42.085 --> 00:01:42.785
goes to zero.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.839
A limit is the value the sums settle

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.245
on, as the strips get thinner.

00:01:47.969 --> 00:01:49.792
The d x reminds us of the strip

00:01:49.853 --> 00:01:50.073
width,

00:01:50.575 --> 00:01:52.418
and a and b are the ends of

00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:52.919
the interval.

00:01:53.724 --> 00:01:54.669
The units come along too.

00:01:55.253 --> 00:01:57.660
Litres per minute, times minutes, gives litres.

00:01:58.403 --> 00:01:59.589
And this works for any rate.

00:02:00.233 --> 00:02:03.178
The sums estimate the total change, so their

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.083
limit is the total change itself.

00:02:05.845 --> 00:02:07.451
For the storm in the last video, it's

00:02:07.573 --> 00:02:08.255
the rain that fell.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.751
For this bath, it's the change in the

00:02:10.812 --> 00:02:11.476
water it holds.

00:02:12.218 --> 00:02:14.561
Here, the integral from zero to eight of

00:02:14.622 --> 00:02:17.546
twelve minus two t, d t, looks like

00:02:17.748 --> 00:02:18.308
thirty-two.

00:02:19.092 --> 00:02:20.077
Let's check that with shapes.

00:02:20.809 --> 00:02:22.958
When the graph makes simple shapes, we can

00:02:22.999 --> 00:02:24.827
find the integral from their areas.

00:02:25.691 --> 00:02:27.652
From zero to six, the graph and the

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:30.395
axis make a triangle, with base six and

00:02:30.436 --> 00:02:31.095
height twelve.

00:02:31.958 --> 00:02:34.668
Half of six, times twelve, is thirty-six.

00:02:35.372 --> 00:02:36.935
So the integral from zero to six

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.438
is thirty-six,

00:02:38.941 --> 00:02:41.065
and the bath gains thirty-six litres.

00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:43.794
From six to eight, the graph is below

00:02:43.856 --> 00:02:44.336
the axis.

00:02:44.999 --> 00:02:47.180
Every strip there is negative, or zero at

00:02:47.201 --> 00:02:50.242
the start, so no sum is positive, and

00:02:50.263 --> 00:02:51.764
the integral can't be positive either.

00:02:52.466 --> 00:02:54.916
This region has real size below the axis,

00:02:55.299 --> 00:02:56.905
so here the integral is negative.

00:02:57.649 --> 00:03:00.116
This triangle has base two and depth four,

00:03:00.498 --> 00:03:01.902
so its area is four.

00:03:02.585 --> 00:03:04.290
So the integral from six to eight is

00:03:04.511 --> 00:03:05.132
minus four.

00:03:05.635 --> 00:03:07.344
The bath loses four litres.

00:03:08.115 --> 00:03:10.443
Over the whole eight minutes, the graph changes

00:03:10.525 --> 00:03:10.825
sign.

00:03:11.388 --> 00:03:13.255
The integral adds the signed pieces.

00:03:13.878 --> 00:03:16.408
Thirty-six, plus minus four, gives thirty-two.

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.566
That matches the settled sums.

00:03:19.314 --> 00:03:20.358
It's the net change:

00:03:20.902 --> 00:03:22.790
the bath ends with thirty-two litres more than

00:03:22.831 --> 00:03:23.473
it started with.

00:03:24.338 --> 00:03:25.823
If it had drained more than it gained,

00:03:25.944 --> 00:03:27.027
the integral would be negative.

00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:30.403
Area above the axis counts as positive, and

00:03:30.504 --> 00:03:32.191
area below counts as negative.

00:03:32.935 --> 00:03:35.303
The shape doesn't have to start at zero.

00:03:35.967 --> 00:03:38.180
Find the integral from one to three of

00:03:38.543 --> 00:03:39.367
two x plus one.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.013
At x equals one, the line is at

00:03:42.074 --> 00:03:44.859
height three, and at x equals three, it's

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:45.561
at height seven.

00:03:46.343 --> 00:03:48.628
The region between the line and the axis,

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.095
from one to three, is a trapezium.

00:03:51.637 --> 00:03:54.042
Its area is the average of three and

00:03:54.124 --> 00:03:56.990
seven, times the width two, which is ten.

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.945
The graph stays above the axis, so the

00:04:00.007 --> 00:04:00.971
integral is ten.

00:04:01.723 --> 00:04:02.489
Here's a surprise.

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:05.508
Find the integral from minus three to three

00:04:05.749 --> 00:04:06.293
of x.

00:04:07.157 --> 00:04:09.105
From minus three to zero, the line is

00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:11.675
below the axis, making a triangle with area

00:04:11.695 --> 00:04:12.418
four and a half.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:15.367
From zero to three, there's a matching triangle

00:04:15.407 --> 00:04:17.092
above, also four and a half.

00:04:17.735 --> 00:04:19.442
So the integral is four and a half,

00:04:19.743 --> 00:04:21.913
minus four and a half, which is zero.

00:04:22.596 --> 00:04:24.797
There's plenty of area here, but the integral

00:04:24.898 --> 00:04:26.979
is zero, because the part above and the

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.240
part below balance.

00:04:28.888 --> 00:04:29.994
Shapes can be curved too.

00:04:30.939 --> 00:04:33.123
Find the integral from minus two to two,

00:04:33.565 --> 00:04:35.950
of minus the square root of four minus

00:04:36.111 --> 00:04:36.571
x squared.

00:04:37.514 --> 00:04:39.358
The square root of four minus x squared

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.504
is the top half of a circle, with

00:04:41.565 --> 00:04:42.145
radius two.

00:04:42.969 --> 00:04:45.176
The minus sign flips it below the axis.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.244
Half the circle's area is a half, times

00:04:48.305 --> 00:04:50.930
pi, times two squared, which is two pi.

00:04:51.894 --> 00:04:54.180
Every strip is below the axis, so the

00:04:54.221 --> 00:04:55.745
integral is minus two pi.

00:04:56.272 --> 00:04:57.205
Here's the rule to remember.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.738
Above adds, below subtracts.

00:05:00.422 --> 00:05:02.788
Every strip keeps its sign, and the definite

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:05.196
integral is what the signed sums settle on.

00:05:05.837 --> 00:05:06.297
One condition:

00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:09.220
every integral here runs from the smaller number,

00:05:09.722 --> 00:05:11.703
a, up to the bigger one, b.

00:05:12.406 --> 00:05:13.960
A later video shows what happens when they

00:05:13.981 --> 00:05:14.223
swap.

00:05:16.951 --> 00:05:17.416
Your turn.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.046
Use areas to evaluate the integral from zero

00:05:21.107 --> 00:05:23.631
to three of x minus five, d x.

00:05:24.296 --> 00:05:25.162
Pause here to answer.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:36.749
Sketch it first.

00:05:37.396 --> 00:05:39.399
At zero the line is at minus five,

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:42.165
and at three it's at minus two, so

00:05:42.206 --> 00:05:43.668
it's below the axis the whole way.

00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:46.877
The shape is a trapezium, with parallel sides

00:05:46.958 --> 00:05:48.842
five and two, and width three.

00:05:49.745 --> 00:05:52.372
Its area is three, times seven over two,

00:05:52.874 --> 00:05:54.176
which is twenty-one over two.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.170
It's below the axis, so the integral is

00:05:57.292 --> 00:05:58.577
minus twenty-one over two.

00:05:59.485 --> 00:06:00.518
Twenty-one over two is wrong.

00:06:00.964 --> 00:06:01.729
It loses the sign.

00:06:03.486 --> 00:06:03.895
Last one.

00:06:04.804 --> 00:06:07.534
Use areas to evaluate the integral from zero

00:06:07.594 --> 00:06:09.903
to six of x minus two, d x.

00:06:10.606 --> 00:06:11.435
Pause here to answer.

00:06:22.209 --> 00:06:24.565
The line crosses the axis at x equals

00:06:24.647 --> 00:06:24.867
two.

00:06:25.571 --> 00:06:27.797
From zero to two, there's a triangle below,

00:06:27.818 --> 00:06:28.840
with area two.

00:06:29.563 --> 00:06:31.867
From two to six, there's a triangle above,

00:06:32.229 --> 00:06:34.292
with base four and height four,

00:06:34.975 --> 00:06:36.276
so its area is eight.

00:06:37.059 --> 00:06:39.669
The integral is eight minus two, which is

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:39.970
six.

00:06:40.837 --> 00:06:41.621
Ten is wrong.

00:06:41.863 --> 00:06:44.055
It adds both areas, and forgets that the

00:06:44.096 --> 00:06:45.484
piece below subtracts.

00:06:47.255 --> 00:06:49.943
So a definite integral is a signed sum,

00:06:50.525 --> 00:06:50.825
settled.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.448
Strips below the axis count against it.

00:06:54.293 --> 00:06:55.398
Now a new question.

00:06:56.122 --> 00:06:59.109
Here's the graph of three minus t, shaded

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:00.552
from zero up to a point x.

00:07:01.757 --> 00:07:04.061
The integral from zero to x gives the

00:07:04.142 --> 00:07:07.289
shaded signed area, and it changes as x

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:07.710
moves.

00:07:08.514 --> 00:07:09.968
How fast does it grow?

00:07:12.695 --> 00:07:13.558
Here are the key notes.

00:07:13.961 --> 00:07:15.508
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:16.011
to copy them.
